<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span><span id="A1.T4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mixed vs. monolingual fine-tuning.</span> Results compare the performance of mixed versus monolingual fine-tuning strategies for <span id="A1.T4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">Llama-3.1-8B</span>. Best values are <span id="A1.T4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bolded</span>. Reported values are Mean (<math id="A1.T4.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> Standard Deviation) across 5 independent generation runs on a hold-out test set of 650 users.</figcaption>
</figure>
